message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a Day of the Dead altar. Such items are generally classified as festive articles under heading 9505, specifically 9505.90 ("Other"). Because the altar is made of wood (MDF), I considered 4420 (wooden ornaments) but concluded that Day of the Dead items are treated as festive articles for a celebrated occasion. Heading 9505 covers festive, carnival or other entertainment articles. The Day of the Dead is a recognized festival, and the altar is used to celebrate it. The Explanatory Notes for 9505 cover articles used for festivals. The relevant subheading is 9505.90.6000 ("Other: Other"), the statistical suffix being 9505.90.6000.

The 9505.90 subheadings are 9505.90.20 (Christmas ornaments? no, that is 9505.10), 9505.90.40 (Articles for magic tricks and practical jokes), 9505.90.60 (Other), so 9505.90.6000 is correct.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The MDF Day of the Dead ofrenda altar is a festive article used to celebrate a recognized festival, so it falls in heading 9505 under the residual subheading for other festive articles."}
